    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "that makes sense. could you give me some specific examples of foods for both categories? like, if i'm at a grocery store, what should i be looking for to keep my levels steady?",
      "source": "evaluator"
    },
    {
      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "For low GI examples, look for whole grains like oats, brown rice, lentils, and most vegetables. High GI examples include white bread, sugary cereals, white pasta, and white rice. To keep your levels steady at the grocery store, always prioritize the \"wholegrain\" versions of starches and focus heavily on fiber-rich vegetables and legumes. These choices will provide sustained energy and a gentler impact on your blood sugar.",
      "source": "target",
